// The props, and the place you were told not to go.

== The Sundial Speaks
  setting: Orchard Gate

Narrator: The gnomon is bent to point at the glasshouse. Somebody bent it
  on purpose.
set guest.suspicion += 10

== The Letterbox
  setting: Orchard Gate

Narrator: Nine invitations, unsent, all in Mara's hand. Yours is not among them.
* Take one.
  set guest.suspicion += 15
  reply You slip an invitation into your pocket. It is addressed to nobody.
+ Leave them.
  set guest.favour += 3

== The Wine Rack
  setting: The Long Table

Narrator: Every bottle is the same year. Every label has been scratched off.
cycle One bottle is warm. | One bottle is missing. | One bottle is full of earth.

== The Cold Frame
  setting: The Glasshouse

Narrator: Seedlings, labelled in two hands. The second hand is shaking.
set guest.suspicion += 10

== The Glasshouse at Night
  setting: The Glasshouse
  cast: Dr Sable Quill

Self: You shouldn't be in here. Nobody should. Look at the roots.

if guest.group == The_Collectors:
  Self: You're one of the key people. Then you already know where the door is.
  set guest.suspicion += 20
else if guest.group == The_Gardeners:
  Self: Rosemary. Good. Then help me. She's under the orchard, and I can't dig.
  set guest.suspicion += 10
else:
  Self: No side yet? Choose one before the toast, or the choice gets made for you.

* Look at the roots.
  Narrator: They run in one direction, all of them. Down.
  set guest.suspicion += 25
* Back away.
  set guest.favour += 5
  -> The Long Table
